From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 03:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: cdnsp-sky1: defer probe on missing clocks instead of failing

Confirmed live on Orion O6N, 2026-07-19: the clk-sky1-acpi bridge fix
(0157) makes sky1_acpi_clk_probe() succeed as soon as ANY CLKT entry
maps, on the theory that consumers whose specific clock is not yet
mapped would get their own retryable -EPROBE_DEFER from devm_clk_get()
and be retried independently (0157s own commit message says exactly
this, and flags itself UNVERIFIED ON HARDWARE). That theory only holds
if the consumer actually propagates -EPROBE_DEFER -- this one instead
returned the raw devm_clk_get() error (-ENOENT, 
o such clkdev\)
straight out of probe. -ENOENT is not -EPROBE_DEFER, so the driver
core never retries it: a clock that legitimately becomes available
moments later (once the bridge or SCMI catches up) is permanently
unavailable to this driver for the rest of the boot.

Same fix already proven working for cix-usbdp-phy (0155) and pwm-sky1
(0158) -- both show as harmless \deferred probe pending\ and
self-resolve later in boot. This applies the identical
-ENOENT-to-EPROBE_DEFER translation via dev_err_probe() to the
remaining consumers that were still hard-failing instead of deferring.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index c43b07d..40e3d2f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -92,7 +92,9 @@ static int sky1_usb_clk_enable_all(struct device *dev)
 	for (i = 0; i < CIX_USB_CLK_NUM; i++) {
 		cix_usb_clks[i] = devm_clk_get(dev, cix_usb_clk_names[i]);
 		if (IS_ERR(cix_usb_clks[i])) {
-			ret = dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(cix_usb_clks[i]),
+			int clk_err = PTR_ERR(cix_usb_clks[i]) == -ENOENT ?
+				-EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(cix_usb_clks[i]);
+			ret = dev_err_probe(dev, clk_err,
 				"could not get %s clock\n", cix_usb_clk_names[i]);
 			goto err_usb_clks;
 		}
@@ -699,7 +701,9 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			struct clk *clk = devm_clk_get(dev,
 						       cix_usb_clk_names[i]);
 			if (IS_ERR(clk))
-				return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk),
+				return dev_err_probe(dev,
+					PTR_ERR(clk) == -ENOENT ?
+					-EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(clk),
 					"could not get %s clock\n",
 					cix_usb_clk_names[i]);
 		}
--
2.51.0
